# Portfolio 4: NoSQL and Advanced Data Models

## Project Title
Laykes Online Store – NoSQL Database Implementation

## Introduction
This portfolio demonstrates the use of MongoDB, a NoSQL document-oriented database, for managing customer orders in Laykes Online Store.

## Database Used
MongoDB Community Server and MongoDB Compass.

## Database Name
laykes_online_store_nosql

## Collection
orders

## Objectives
- Understand NoSQL database concepts.
- Create a document-based data model.
- Insert and retrieve customer order documents.
- Demonstrate how MongoDB stores related information in documents.
- Compare relational databases with NoSQL databases.

## Implementation
The database contains customer order documents with customer details, products, payment status, delivery status and order amounts.

## Conclusion
MongoDB provides a flexible way to store related order information in a document. This approach is useful for e-commerce applications such as Laykes Online Store.
